WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.350 --> 00:00:05.455
Hello, everyone! I'm Ms. Emma. Welcome to Online Newspaper Class, level two.

2
00:00:05.755 --> 00:00:09.338
Hi! I'm Visal. Let's learn together!

3
00:00:09.638 --> 00:00:15.797
Unit thirteen: Mergers & Acquisitions. Today you will report claims with passive reporting structures.

4
00:00:16.097 --> 00:00:18.831
Here is our lesson map. Let's start!

5
00:00:19.767 --> 00:00:23.000
Part one: words. You will learn eight new words.

6
00:00:23.850 --> 00:00:25.443
Acquisition target.

7
00:00:26.450 --> 00:00:30.133
Acquisition target means a company that another company wants to buy.

8
00:00:30.717 --> 00:00:33.297
The small brewer became an acquisition target.

9
00:00:33.883 --> 00:00:37.081
Your turn. Say: Acquisition target.

10
00:00:39.933 --> 00:00:41.747
Acquisition target.

11
00:00:42.483 --> 00:00:43.670
Due diligence.

12
00:00:44.683 --> 00:00:48.842
Due diligence means a careful check of a company's finances before buying it.

13
00:00:49.450 --> 00:00:51.751
Due diligence revealed hidden debts.

14
00:00:52.350 --> 00:00:55.188
Your turn. Say: Due diligence.

15
00:00:58.033 --> 00:00:59.313
Due diligence.

16
00:01:00.050 --> 00:01:01.411
Hostile takeover.

17
00:01:02.417 --> 00:01:06.878
Hostile takeover means an attempt to buy a company against its management's wishes.

18
00:01:07.483 --> 00:01:09.564
The board fought the hostile takeover.

19
00:01:10.150 --> 00:01:12.791
Your turn. Say: Hostile takeover.

20
00:01:15.633 --> 00:01:17.029
Hostile takeover.

21
00:01:17.783 --> 00:01:18.552
Synergy.

22
00:01:19.550 --> 00:01:23.651
Synergy means extra value created when two companies work together.

23
00:01:24.250 --> 00:01:26.424
The merger promised synergy in marketing.

24
00:01:27.017 --> 00:01:29.402
Your turn. Say: Synergy.

25
00:01:32.267 --> 00:01:33.210
Synergy.

26
00:01:33.950 --> 00:01:35.253
Deal valuation.

27
00:01:36.250 --> 00:01:40.014
Deal valuation means the price put on a company in a merger or sale.

28
00:01:40.617 --> 00:01:43.266
The deal valuation was higher than expected.

29
00:01:43.850 --> 00:01:46.851
Your turn. Say: Deal valuation.

30
00:01:49.700 --> 00:01:51.119
Deal valuation.

31
00:01:51.883 --> 00:01:53.407
Regulatory approval.

32
00:01:54.417 --> 00:01:58.471
Regulatory approval means official permission needed to complete a deal.

33
00:01:59.083 --> 00:02:01.617
Regulatory approval took six months.

34
00:02:02.217 --> 00:02:05.484
Your turn. Say: Regulatory approval.

35
00:02:08.333 --> 00:02:10.124
Regulatory approval.

36
00:02:10.883 --> 00:02:12.001
Shareholder vote.

37
00:02:13.017 --> 00:02:16.978
Shareholder vote means a formal decision made by the owners of a company.

38
00:02:17.583 --> 00:02:20.140
A shareholder vote approved the merger.

39
00:02:20.750 --> 00:02:23.565
Your turn. Say: Shareholder vote.

40
00:02:26.400 --> 00:02:27.564
Shareholder vote.

41
00:02:28.317 --> 00:02:30.049
Integration process.

42
00:02:31.050 --> 00:02:35.395
Integration process means combining the people and systems of two companies.

43
00:02:35.983 --> 00:02:38.645
The integration process lasted two years.

44
00:02:39.250 --> 00:02:42.448
Your turn. Say: Integration process.

45
00:02:45.300 --> 00:02:46.963
Integration process.

46
00:02:47.767 --> 00:02:51.197
Part two: dialogue. Let's listen to a conversation.

47
00:02:52.050 --> 00:03:00.104
Visal, a headline says 'The merger is expected to create synergy.' But another says 'It is said that jobs will be cut.' What are these patterns?

48
00:03:01.217 --> 00:03:09.950
Passive reporting structures: it is said that..., the merger is expected to... They report opinions without naming who holds them.

49
00:03:11.050 --> 00:03:13.108
Why use them in business news?

50
00:03:14.217 --> 00:03:22.361
Because reporters often cannot prove a claim. 'The firm is believed to be an acquisition target' is more careful than a flat statement.

51
00:03:23.450 --> 00:03:25.403
Can synergy always be trusted?

52
00:03:26.517 --> 00:03:37.377
Not always. After due diligence, a valuation and a shareholder vote, the integration process may reveal that promised savings were exaggerated.

53
00:03:38.533 --> 00:03:40.161
Part three: grammar.

54
00:03:41.017 --> 00:03:45.234
Grammar focus: Passive reporting: is said to and it is believed that.

55
00:03:45.534 --> 00:03:46.883
Look at the pattern.

56
00:03:47.583 --> 00:03:49.978
The merger is expected to create synergy.

57
00:03:50.883 --> 00:03:53.870
It is believed that the firm is an acquisition target.

58
00:03:54.783 --> 00:03:57.433
The bidder is said to have offered a high valuation.

59
00:03:58.367 --> 00:04:06.151
Use subject + is said / believed / expected to + verb, or It is said that + clause. For past events use to have + past participle.

60
00:04:06.917 --> 00:04:10.475
Be careful! Don't say: It said that he resign.

61
00:04:12.433 --> 00:04:14.700
Say: It is said that he resigned.

62
00:04:15.000 --> 00:04:17.603
Use the passive: it is said that...

63
00:04:18.400 --> 00:04:20.832
Part four: reading. Read and listen.

64
00:04:21.633 --> 00:04:22.797
Behind the Deal.

65
00:04:23.097 --> 00:04:26.107
Merger announcements often promise more than they deliver.

66
00:04:27.100 --> 00:04:34.185
A company is believed to be an acquisition target when rivals show interest, and a hostile takeover is said to be the most aggressive route.

67
00:04:35.200 --> 00:04:40.903
Due diligence is meant to reveal hidden risks, yet the deal valuation may still be too high.

68
00:04:41.900 --> 00:04:46.848
After regulatory approval and a shareholder vote, the integration process begins.

69
00:04:47.833 --> 00:04:51.342
Synergy is often promised, but it is not always achieved.

70
00:04:52.433 --> 00:04:56.168
Part five: quiz. Five questions. Are you ready?

71
00:04:57.017 --> 00:04:58.993
The merger blank to create synergy.

72
00:04:59.293 --> 00:05:03.469
A, is expected. B, expects. C, is expecting.

73
00:05:07.033 --> 00:05:09.439
The answer is A: is expected.

74
00:05:10.583 --> 00:05:14.034
A careful check of a company's finances is blank diligence.

75
00:05:14.334 --> 00:05:17.453
A, late. B, due. C, hostile.

76
00:05:21.000 --> 00:05:23.034
The answer is B: due.

77
00:05:24.183 --> 00:05:27.379
Extra value from two companies working together is blank.

78
00:05:27.679 --> 00:05:31.808
A, valuation. B, approval. C, synergy.

79
00:05:35.367 --> 00:05:37.215
The answer is C: synergy.

80
00:05:38.350 --> 00:05:40.036
Choose the correct sentence.

81
00:05:40.336 --> 00:05:46.660
A, It is said that he has resigned.. B, It said that he has resign.. C, It is saying that he resigned..

82
00:05:50.200 --> 00:05:53.244
The answer is A: It is said that he has resigned..

83
00:05:54.383 --> 00:05:58.101
According to the reading, synergy is often promised but not always…

84
00:05:58.401 --> 00:06:01.846
A, achieved. B, spoken. C, valued.

85
00:06:05.400 --> 00:06:07.179
The answer is A: achieved.

86
00:06:08.367 --> 00:06:11.553
Part six: speaking. It's your turn to talk.

87
00:06:12.417 --> 00:06:17.957
Why might two companies claim a merger will create 'synergy,' and is that always true?

88
00:06:26.750 --> 00:06:28.401
Now listen to Visal.

89
00:06:28.701 --> 00:06:55.821
Companies claim synergy because it persuades shareholders and regulators that a merger will bring savings or new sales. Sometimes it is true, for example when two firms share a distribution network. However, cultures may clash and systems may not fit, so promised savings often disappear. Therefore, I would treat such claims with caution.

90
00:06:56.121 --> 00:06:57.819
Excellent answer, Visal!

91
00:06:58.717 --> 00:07:04.736
Great work! Now you can use eight new words and passive reporting: is said to and it is believed that.

92
00:07:05.036 --> 00:07:09.906
Today's value is critical thinking. Think carefully and give reasons for your opinions.

93
00:07:10.206 --> 00:07:12.893
See you in Unit fourteen. Goodbye!

94
00:07:13.193 --> 00:07:15.694
Thank you, Ms. Emma! Bye, everyone!

